{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 131, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual shortcut where none existed helps far more than replacing an existing op (exp 15 vs 16-18, 19 vs 20-21, 77 vs 78)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the only direct conv on the input-output path with identity removes capacity and hurts badly (exp 20, 24, 78)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-output path gives large gains, while replacing an existing skip loses the residual (exp 97-98 vs 99-100)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a missing node1-output path gains more than replacing a skip on it (exp 63, 65 vs 64, 66)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Opening the node2-output path makes node 2's computation useful, so gains exceed op swaps (exp 1, 5, 74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 4 leaves only edge 3 feeding the output, which collapses accuracy (exp 89, 91 vs 90, 92)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the skip when edge 5 is absent leaves edge 4 as the only output input (exp 25, 30 vs 26, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 1 feeds node 2, which cannot reach the output without edge 5, so the conv adds little (exp 85 vs 86, 87 vs 88)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher",